                <pb facs="0917" n="791" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg791"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.00/93</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The British Chargé</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chilton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Manchester, Mass.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-07-20"><hi rendition="#italic">July 20,
                        1925.</hi></date><lb/>[Received July 21.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 703</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honour to refer to my
                    immediately preceding notes regarding the reply to be returned by the Diplomatic
                    Body at Peking to the representations addressed to them by the Chinese
                    Government on June 24th last.</p>
                <p>His Majesty’s Government now inform me that the Italian proposal, to which
                    reference was made in paragraph two of my note No. 701, is that the identic
                    reply by the Powers to the above-mentioned Chinese representations should embody
                    and itself constitute the public declaration previously suggested by His
                    Majesty’s Government.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>(For His Majesty’s Minister)<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John
                            Balfour</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
